  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given equation of ellipse is\r\n$$\r\n16 x^{2}+25 y^{2}+32 x-100 y=284\r\n$$\r\nSimplifying the given equation, we have ellipse as\r\n$$\r\n\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{16}=1\r\n$$\r\nSo, the auxiliary equation of circle is\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{r}\r\n(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=25 \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow \\quad x^{2}+2 x+1+y^{2}-4 y+4=25\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\n$\\therefore$\r\n$x^{2}+y^{2}+2 x-4 y-20=0$",
    "image": null
  },
